{
  "acceptanceResults": [
    "Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock consistently identify version 0.2.91 with no unrelated dependency changes.",
    "The three WI-801 Work Item pages and tri-language parity rows are registered before verification.",
    "Release preflight, source quality, candidate build and immutable public/N-1 acceptance can bind the published v0.2.91 artifacts to reviewed main.",
    "The canonical workspace package gate must use bounded package-level parallelism and configurable in-package test threads while preserving deterministic package ordering, fail-closed omission reporting, metadata failure reporting, and compatibility with the existing gate manifest.",
    "All current release/version/reference projections update the workspace version, previous public baseline, reviewed Runtime version, Runtime digest, and reviewed baseline together in all three supported languages.",
    "The CI quality route and release preflight execute the real source version-consistency check before expensive workspace, candidate, or adopter verification; the static policy regression remains covered separately.",
    "A clean checkout of the reviewed branch passes the same cheap version and documentation acceptance gates used by hosted CI, so local workspace state cannot hide stale projections.",
    "Runtime-bound verification refreshes governance with the same Runtime identity as preflight, so a passed verification cannot rewrite a valid current preflight decision into stale evidence",
    "A regression test covers current-Runtime preflight, checkpoint, verification, and the subsequent preflight/finish boundary",
    "Acceptance recovery consumes the Rust strategy for every retry: blocked strategies cannot record success, cleanup-only recovery performs only the exact cleanup target, and a missing or incomplete resume receipt fails closed instead of creating an empty plan.",
    "Phase receipts reject contradictory success/failure fields and concurrent updates preserve append-only history through a repository-local transaction boundary.",
    "Release preflight and source quality persist structured failure evidence on early failure, and immutable artifact reuse does not overwrite prior attempt evidence.",
    "Release close requires a successful public N-1 receipt or a valid not-applicable receipt; skipped upstream jobs and incomplete phase bindings block close.",
    "N-1 resolution selects only a published version lower than the target version, and public acceptance can recover the exact prior publication handoff without rerunning publication.",
    "Isolation manifests use the Rust single-process scanner in production; the legacy shell implementation is retained only for explicit equivalence regression coverage.",
    "All regression assertions changed by the Rust release-route migration remain Contract-scoped and execute before hosted release work begins."
  ],
